{"name":"Sea Goddess","hex":"#216987","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sea goddess","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A female sea god.","Any of certain nudibranchs."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sea_goddess"}],"entries":[{"title":"List of water deities","blocks":[{"text":"A water deity is a deity in mythology associated with water or various bodies of water. Water deities are common in mythology and were usually more important among civilizations in which the sea or ocean, or a great river was more important. Another important focus of worship of water deities has been springs or holy wells."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Gaziantep_Zeugma_Museum_Water_gods_mosaic_8199.jpg/330px-Gaziantep_Zeugma_Museum_Water_gods_mosaic_8199.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_water_deities"},{"title":"Sea","blocks":[{"text":"A sea is a very large body of salty water. The term has two distinct meanings. The first is the interconnected body of seawater that spans most of Earth, known as the sea or the ocean. The second is a named body of water: usually either a marginal sea, or a large, nearly landlocked body of water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg/330px-Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea"},{"title":"Goddess","blocks":[{"text":"A goddess is a female deity. In some faiths, a sacred female figure holds a central place in religious prayer and worship. For example, Shaktism, holds that the ultimate deity, the source of all reality, is Supreme Goddess (Mahamaya) and in some forms of Tantric Shaivism, the pair of Shiva and Shakti are the ultimate principle. Meanwhile, in Vajrayana Buddhism, ultimate reality is often seen as being composed of two principles depicted as two deities in union symbolising the non-duality of the two principles of perfect wisdom (female) and skillful compassion (male). A single figure in a monotheistic faith that is female may be identified simply as god because of no need to differentiate by gender or with a diminutive. An experiment to determine the effect of psychedelics on subjects composed of leaders from diverse religious groups revealed a general experience that the divine which the subjects encountered was feminine."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Queen_Nefertari_being_led_by_Isis_MET_DP167142.jpg/330px-Queen_Nefertari_being_led_by_Isis_MET_DP167142.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goddess"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/%E9%B9%BF%E6%B8%AF%E6%96%B0%E7%A5%96%E5%AE%AE%E3%80%8C%E6%85%B6%E7%AB%AF%E9%99%BD%E6%B4%BB%E5%8B%95%E3%80%8D.jpg/500px-%E9%B9%BF%E6%B8%AF%E6%96%B0%E7%A5%96%E5%AE%AE%E3%80%8C%E6%85%B6%E7%AB%AF%E9%99%BD%E6%B4%BB%E5%8B%95%E3%80%8D.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/%E9%B9%BF%E6%B8%AF%E6%96%B0%E7%A5%96%E5%AE%AE%E3%80%8C%E6%85%B6%E7%AB%AF%E9%99%BD%E6%B4%BB%E5%8B%95%E3%80%8D.jpg/1280px-%E9%B9%BF%E6%B8%AF%E6%96%B0%E7%A5%96%E5%AE%AE%E3%80%8C%E6%85%B6%E7%AB%AF%E9%99%BD%E6%B4%BB%E5%8B%95%E3%80%8D.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/%E9%B9%BF%E6%B8%AF%E6%96%B0%E7%A5%96%E5%AE%AE%E3%80%8C%E6%85%B6%E7%AB%AF%E9%99%BD%E6%B4%BB%E5%8B%95%E3%80%8D.jpg/500px-%E9%B9%BF%E6%B8%AF%E6%96%B0%E7%A5%96%E5%AE%AE%E3%80%8C%E6%85%B6%E7%AB%AF%E9%99%BD%E6%B4%BB%E5%8B%95%E3%80%8D.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Chinese sea goddess Mazu","link":"https://en.